<title>RUSSIA: Russia Jan-Nov oil output down 2.0 pct, exports up.</title>
<headline>Russia Jan-Nov oil output down 2.0 pct, exports up.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian crude oil output in the first 11 months of the year fell to 275.9 million tonnes including gas condensate in the oil, a two percent drop on a year ago, the Fuel and Energy Ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>A ministry press release said crude oil exports over January-November, including to Baltic states but not to members of the Commonwealth of Independent States (CIS), increased to 92.8 million tonnes, 4.7 percent higher than a year ago.</p>
<p>The ministry released the following figures for Russian energy output:</p>
<p>		   Jan-Nov 1996 energy production</p>
<p>		   in million     yr/yr change</p>
<p>		     tonnes     percent  million tonnes</p>
<p>Crude oil with</p>
<p>  gas condensate  275.9	-2.0	-5.2</p>
<p> Refined oil	161.4	-3.9	-6.6</p>
<p> Natural gas	545.3	+1.1	+6.0</p>
<p>(billion cubic</p>
<p>metres)</p>
<p>		     Jan-Nov 1996 oil export</p>
<p>		   in million     yr/yr</p>
<p>		     tonnes     pct change</p>
<p>Crude oil</p>
<p>  non-CIS	    92.8	+4.7</p>
<p>  CIS		  19.8     -15.6</p>
<p>-- Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
